  "implementation_notes": "Keep DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, all four independently routed categories, unchanged splits, and SASREC_EPOCHS default 200. Preserve baseline dimensions, optimizer, batching, and scheduler for the initial controlled comparisons; serialize their resolved values and all new settings. Write checkpoints and generated predictor files beneath the trial directory and keep execution single-GPU. No experiment has been run and no improvement is established.\n\nAt every valid supervised position, pool input item embeddings at lags 0 through 4, masking padding and unavailable earlier positions before normalizing weights proportional to exp(-softplus(theta) * lag). Lag 0 is the current input, not the next-item target. Initialize softplus(theta) to log(2)/2, giving an initial two-event half-life. This uses event lag, not elapsed time. Do not claim timestamp modeling; timestamp inputs would require a separate ablation. Use the shared item embedding table. Let r_raw denote the pooled vector and use r = r_raw * stopgrad(||h||_2) / max(||r_raw||_2, 1e-8). This preserves the baseline h branch and matches branch magnitudes approximately, except for near-zero vectors. Define the gate as Linear(3d,d), GELU, Linear(d,1), sigmoid; initialize the final layer's weights to zero and bias to -2. Score with the unchanged shared item embeddings using features h + g*r. Log pre-matching branch norms, the norm ratio, gate mean, and fractions below 0.05 and above 0.95; these thresholds are diagnostic conventions, not demonstrated failure criteria.\n\nUse each user's entire observed training history as the negative exclusion set, including items later than a particular training prefix. This is a training-only sampling policy, not additional encoder input; document that it differs from prefix-only exclusion. Do not consult validation or test interactions. For each valid target, sample k=min(32,M) unique uniform negatives without replacement from its eligible pool of size M. Mask padded candidate logits with negative infinity, average over valid targets with k>0, and skip optimization for batches with no eligible targets. Record the frequency of reduced-k and skipped targets. Efficient rejection sampling must fall back to an explicit eligible pool when rejection becomes excessive without changing uniformity.\n\nDefine loss explicitly as -s_positive + logsumexp(s_positive, s_negative_1, ..., s_negative_k), without sampling correction. It is a sampled ranking objective, not an exact full-catalog softmax estimator. If an importance-weighted alternative is later tested, treat it as a different objective: shift each negative by log(M/k), leave the positive unchanged, and recognize that history exclusion restricts the estimated denominator. Do not silently mix these formulations. For memory-limited chunking, initialize the accumulator with the positive logit, merge every negative chunk through logaddexp and logsumexp in FP32, and subtract the positive only after the final merge. Preserve autograd; summing separate chunk losses changes the objective.\n\nPredeclare a staged comparison: baseline versus objective-only; then fixed gate sigmoid(-2), learned global scalar gate, and contextual gate with identical window and normalization. The scalar and contextual gates begin at the same value. Report parameter counts; use a parameter-matched state-only gate control if attributing gains specifically to recent-state conditioning, since the simpler controls do not themselves match capacity. Compare uniform pooling against learned decay only after the primary comparison. Use the same category initialization seed and separate seeded negative-sampling generator where feasible. Track training cost and prioritize these controls within the shared 43,200 GPU-second budget rather than promising an exhaustive grid.\n\nBefore running, fix validation cadence to every ten epochs and select the checkpoint with highest pinned four-category macro HR@10, breaking ties toward the earlier epoch. This checkpoint policy is a proposed reproducible choice, not a statement about the original baseline. Compare controls under the same policy and archive per-category scores and per-user hit indicators when exposed by the authorized evaluator. Do not change the evaluator to obtain additional output. If paired hits are available, bootstrap 200 users with replacement independently within each category, preserving baseline–variant pairing, average the four category differences, and use 10,000 replicates with a separate fixed diagnostic seed. Percentile intervals condition on fixed models and candidates; they omit seed variability and do not correct checkpoint or hyperparameter selection optimism. An interval crossing zero means unresolved improvement, not equivalence. Category and timestamp-gap summaries are exploratory and may be noisy. Use only training-history timestamps to define gap strata. Do not infer purchase-intent labels.\n\nPreserve DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis), returning measured metrics and their definitions. view.model must be the actual trained module; view.item_emb remains its shared item embedding table. log2feats(sequence) must return the combined features used for scoring, and predict_score(features, items) must use the same dot product as training and inference. Retain compatibility with batches (None, sequence, positive, negative), even though training now draws additional negatives internally. Existing margin diagnostics may continue using the loader's negatives, but disclose that distribution and preserve definitions; their values are not directly the multi-negative training objective. Measure embedding similarity on actual item embeddings. Metadata category breakdowns are unavailable in this task and must be reported as unavailable, not fabricated. Keep review_data empty when unavailable