Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probe accesses item embeddings through `item_emb.weight` and sequence 
representations through `log2feats(sequence)`. It passes these features and 
candidate item IDs to `predict_score` for positive/negative logits at each 
sequence position. The supplied code does not show the model architecture or how
a final user representation is computed; diagnosis evaluates per-position 
features rather than explicitly selecting the last position.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(model, device)` stores the supplied model or compatibility view,
plus `meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`. Only metadata is subsequently
read; stored reviews and histories are unused.

The loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with tensors shaped 
`B × L`. The probe examines at most ten batches, converts sequences to NumPy, 
computes features, stacks candidate IDs into `B × L × 2`, and scores them. 
Positions with positive item ID zero are excluded. Scoring runs in evaluation 
mode without gradients.

# Probes & Metrics

- **`embedding_collapse_score`**: Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding item embeddings
using seed 42, normalizes them, averages off-diagonal cosine similarities, and 
maps the result to `[0,1]`. Higher values indicate directional alignment; 
orthogonal embeddings score approximately 0.5. This measures alignment, not 
recommendation diversity directly.
- **`pos_neg_margin_mean` / `pos_neg_margin_p10`**: Mean and lower tenth 
percentile of positive minus negative logits. Larger values suggest stronger 
separation.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`**: Fraction with negative margins. Lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`**: Fraction with margins below 0.5. Lower 
indicates fewer weakly separated examples.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`**: Counts categories separately for 
positive and negative items in low-margin and wrong-ranking cases, retaining the
top twenty categories.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence perturbation, shuffling, ablation, or sensitivity test occurs. 
Random embedding sampling only limits computation.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both in instructions requesting JSON with 
`status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and `evidence`; it does not 
itself generate that interpretation.

Category metadata is unavailable under this task, so category lists remain 
empty. The probes do not measure validation HR@10, generalization, temporal 
sensitivity, gradients, full-catalog ranking, or simulator traits. Results 
depend on sampled training negatives and logit scale. Evaluation mode is not 
restored afterward.

