INFO:self_evolverec:The new idea for model in iteration 1:
{
  "description": "Recent-support residual SASRec with sequence-shared uniform sampled cross-entropy. Add a baseline-preserving, gated mean of recent item embeddings to causal SASRec features, and train next-item classification against multiple eligible alternatives.",
  "motivation": "The user diagnosis identifies two eligible targets: stale or isolated interactions being treated as current demand, and broad similarity producing recommendations without specific recent support. Recent pooling provides an explicit local-evidence path, while a learned gate permits the existing history representation to remain dominant. The model diagnosis identifies weak positive–negative separation, especially Electronics' 14.95% wrong-ranking rate and negative margin p10; multi-negative cross-entropy addresses candidate discrimination. SASRec already models recency, so additional benefit must be demonstrated. Neither mechanism establishes compatibility, confirmed ownership, replacement demand, or satisfaction of a durable-device need; uncertain recommendations must remain distinct from explicit mismatches.",
  "implementation_notes": "Preserve DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, all four category routes, original splits, and trial-local artifacts. Respect SASREC_EPOCHS, whose supplied default is 200. Do not download weights or datasets. Only public histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps are eligible; ignore the generic examples listing unavailable ratings, reviews, categories, prices, or stores. Simulator diversity and conformity traits remain unobserved.\n\nArchitecture: retain the original SASRec encoder, item embeddings, positional representation, normalization, and scoring scale. Let h_t be its original output and r_t the masked mean of the embeddings for observed positions max(1,t−4) through t. Exclude padding and return zero for an empty window. Use g_t = sigmoid(aᵀ concat(h_t,r_t) + b), with a initialized to zero and b = −2. Set z_t = h_t + g_t * (W_r r_t + c_r), initializing W_r and c_r to zero. Add no post-fusion LayerNorm. This produces exactly the original features at initialization; verify matching evaluation-mode scores with identical backbone weights and branch enabled versus disabled. Do not zero both the gate output and projection, which would block learning. The projection can learn immediately; gate parameters begin learning after the projection becomes nonzero. Pool only observed inputs through t; the shifted target at t+1 never enters r_t.\n\nSampling and loss: build each user's exclusion set from the complete available training history, including shifted training targets. Never inspect held-out interactions for exclusions. For each sampled sequence, draw K_u = min(64, number_of_eligible_items) unique uniform negatives without replacement from IDs 1..item_count outside that exclusion set. Reuse that sequence's negatives at all valid timesteps; refresh them on the next training draw. Use rejection sampling with a local seeded generator and an explicit eligible-list fallback when acceptance becomes inefficient. Skip and log sequences with no eligible negatives. Score the positive in column zero and that sequence's negatives in the remaining columns; average ordinary cross-entropy over nonpadding target positions. Unique sampling avoids accidental duplicate weighting in the denominator. This defines sampled candidate classification, not an unbiased estimate of unrestricted full-catalog softmax. No LogQ correction is part of this chosen objective. Chunk score computation while preserving the global valid-position mean and gradients. Keep backbone hyperparameters, optimizer, regularization, batch size, sequence length, training sampler, and learning-rate schedule identical to the supplied baseline unless explicitly registered as a separate trial.\n\nEvaluation and budget: predeclare four primary configurations—unchanged SASRec, objective-only, fusion-only using the original BCE, and combined—and use identical checkpoint cadence, for example every 10 completed epochs through the configured limit. Establish equal per-configuration GPU-time caps before execution, reserving measured validation and diagnosis costs within the shared 43,200 GPU-second budget; all failed trials count. Record completed epochs and updates because equal GPU time can mean unequal optimization steps. Select checkpoints and complete four-route configurations exclusively by pinned macro validation HR@10. For exact ties, prefer the simpler configuration, then the earlier checkpoint, then a fixed configuration order. Report neighboring evaluated checkpoints, category HR values, elapsed GPU time, failures, and the complete selection record. Do not claim that an unexecuted configuration completed or improved results.\n\nIf the budget permits, prioritize a fixed-gate recent-mean control and a last-item residual to test whether learned fusion improves on a recency shortcut. Further registered controls are full-history mean, a training-frequency popularity-only score adjustment, and window sizes 1/5/10. A normalization-only control becomes necessary if normalization is changed. These are optional experiments, not required evidence already obtained. Avoid a broad adaptive search over them. Report head/tail slices using a predeclared cutoff derived only from training frequencies, with slice sample sizes; they are diagnostic and do not replace the macro selection metric.\n\nWhere the pinned evaluator exposes per-user hits, retain paired candidate and baseline hits for the same 200 users/category and fixed candidate sets. Use 10,000 bootstrap replicates with a separate analysis RNG seed 42: independently resample paired users within each category, compute each category's mean hit difference, and equally average the four differences. Report the observed macro difference, percentile 95% interval, and category differences. One hit changes category HR by 0.005 and macro HR by 0.00125. The interval conditions on the trained models and fixed candidates; it excludes training randomness, candidate variability, and adaptive selection optimism. If per-user outputs are unavailable, report that limitation rather than modifying the host evaluator or inventing intervals. Sampled HR@10 does not establish full-catalog quality.\n\nSerialization and diagnostics: update both checkpoint configuration and the predictor writer so working/predict.py reconstructs the pooling, gate, projection, and category routing exactly. Save window size, backbone configuration, item mappings, and state_dict beneath the trial directory. Preserve DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis), returning measured metrics and their definitions. view.model must be the actual trained module; view.item_emb remains its item table, view.log2feats returns z, and view.predict_score performs the actual shared-embedding scoring. Preserve the supplied margin and embedding-similarity definitions and diagnostic sampling procedure for comparability. Category breakdowns must be explicitly unavailable, not inferred or fabricated. Diagnostics use training data only and remain separate from selection. Twenty real training users, five/category, still receive full-catalog unseen-item recommendations through the native simulator. Preserve qualitative distinctions between immediate choice, conditional appeal, explicit mismatch, and uncertainty; do not manufacture numeric simulator acceptance or trait measurements.",
  "pseudocode": "register primary_configs = [baseline, objective_only, fusion_only, combined]\nregister checkpoint_cadence, tie_rules, GPU_time_caps, baseline_hyperparameters\nfor configuration in primary_configs:\n    for category in four_categories:\n        initialize baseline backbone using prescribed seed 42\n        if fusion_enabled:\n            initialize gate_weights=0, gate_bias=-2\n            initialize recent_projection_weight=0, recent_projection_bias=0\n            verify initial eval scores match the same backbone without fusion\n        for epoch in configured_epochs subject to registered GPU-time cap:\n            for user_ids, sequence, positive, original_negative in baseline_batches:\n                h = original_causal_sasrec(sequence)\n                if fusion_enabled:\n                    r = causal_nonpadding_embedding_mean(sequence, window=5)\n                    g = sigmoid(gate(concat(h, r)))\n                    z = h + g * recent_projection(r)\n                else:\n                    z = h\n                if sampled_CE_enabled:\n                    for user in batch:\n                        eligible = catalog_ids_without_padding - complete_training_history[user]\n                        K_user = min(64, len(eligible))\n                        negatives[user] = uniform_unique_sample(eligible, K_user)\n                    logits = positive_and_sequence_shared_negative_scores(z)\n                    loss = summed_CE_over_valid_targets_with_eligible_negatives / valid_target_count\n                else:\n                    loss = unchanged_baseline_BCE(z, positive, original_negative)\n                optimizer_step(loss)\n            at registered checkpoints:\n                obtain pinned validation macro and category HR10 without altering evaluator\n                log checkpoint, updates, GPU_time, and available paired user hits\n        save routed model configuration, weights, and matching predictor beneath trial\nselect completed eligible configuration/checkpoint using registered macro-HR10 and tie rules\nreport all trials, category results, checkpoint neighborhoods, and conditional paired uncertainty if available\nrun required training-only diagnostics using actual fused features\nleave held-out test evaluation to host",
