{
  "description": "Add a learned scalar residual gate per dataset that supplements baseline SASRec states with normalized, causally computed recency-weighted item-embedding means. Compare it with matched pooling and fixed-mixture controls before attributing any benefit to gating.",
  "motivation": "Qualitative feedback suggests recent and repeated interests may be underused, but does not establish the correct recency strength. A minimal aggregation branch tests this hypothesis without inferring unavailable traits, ownership, compatibility, or current intent. Existing gating and pooling precedents reduce the novelty claim.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain Movies_and_TV, Industrial_and_Scientific, Electronics, and CDs_and_Vinyl and their routing. Keep DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, and SASREC_EPOCHS default 200. Write artifacts beneath the trial directory and use one GPU. Preserve baseline preprocessing, splits, loss, optimizer, dimensions, sampling, and causal attention. Pool only observed prefix events, retaining repeated IDs as separate occurrences. Maintain FP32 S and Z, update S=a*S+x and Z=a*Z+1 only on valid events, divide by Z.clamp_min(eps), and zero padded outputs. Use a=0.9 for decay and a=1 for uniform pooling; timestamps are unused. Fuse z=h+tanh(g)*LayerNorm(pool), remasking after normalization; initialize one scalar g per dataset to 0.001. Preserve the existing normalization of h without inserting another LayerNorm. The proposed residual approximates baseline behavior at initialization; g=0 reproduces its features exactly. Run the seven prespecified arms in the report, capped at 5,400 GPU-seconds each with 5,400 reserved for diagnostics and failures. Evaluate every ten completed epochs and at termination; stop after four scheduled checks without strict improvement. Choose by pinned four-category macro validation HR@10, breaking ties by earlier checkpoint and then listed arm order. Record every attempted run and checkpoint comparison. Save gate, normalization, decay, arm, baseline configuration, and weights; update the predictor writer so working/predict.py reconstructs identical features and scoring. Verify float64 prefix-reference agreement, causality, padding, repeated events, finite gradients, training/prediction feature parity with dropout disabled, and reload parity. Preserve DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Expose the actual nn.Module through view.model, mixed per-position features through log2feats, and compatible item_emb and predict_score. Return metrics and explicit metric_definitions, distinguish per-position training diagnostics from final-position ranking, and restore the prior train/eval mode even if a probe fails. Report unavailable probes as unavailable with reasons; do not fabricate category breakdowns or subjective acceptance metrics. For supplementary shuffle diagnostics, hold candidates and the last interaction fixed and record the shuffle seed. Report category and macro hits, paired bootstrap differences, popularity/history-length strata, and conditional uncertainty without claiming correction for adaptive selection. Full-catalog recommendations for five training users per category are exposure audits, not accuracy estimates. Never read hidden test files or fetch extra data or pretrained weights. No measured improvements are claimed.",
  "pseudocode": "Prespecify arms = [baseline, mean_only, decay_only, last_item_only, fixed_decay_residual, learned_uniform_residual, learned_decay_residual].\nFor each arm, train all four dataset models sequentially on one GPU under the arm's total compute cap:\n  retain baseline training settings and seeds\n  initialize scalar gate g=0.001 where applicable\n  for each training batch:\n    valid = sequence != 0\n    x = item_emb(sequence)\n    h = baseline_SASRec(sequence)\n    pool = causal_FP32_prefix_mean(x, valid, a), skipping padding updates\n    p = LayerNorm(pool) * valid[..., None]\n    baseline: z = h\n    mean_only or decay_only: z = p\n    last_item_only: z = LayerNorm(x) * valid[..., None]\n    fixed_decay_residual: z = h + 0.1*p\n    learned residual: z = h + tanh(g)*p\n    remask z; score positives and negatives with baseline item embeddings\n    optimize the unchanged baseline loss on valid target positions\n  evaluate at prespecified checkpoints using unchanged pinned validation candidates\n  save complete architecture configuration and checkpoint\nSelect by macro validation HR@10, then earlier checkpoint, then listed arm order.\nUpdate predictor writer and verify reload/training-path parity.\nReport all trials, failures, compute, category scores, and paired category-stratified bootstrap differences; do not interpret selected-winner intervals as search-adjusted.",
