ons and eligible-pool statistics. Unknown positives remain possible. Use temperature 1 and mean loss over valid positions; mask variable candidate padding with negative infinity. Chunk positions to bound memory. Baseline reproduction retains its original sampling; an additional matched-pool one-negative BCE control separates exclusion effects from objective effects.\n\nCall the primary loss uncorrected candidate cross-entropy. Do not claim that uniform sampling makes positive/negative correction cancel. A separate corrected eligible-set experiment adds log(M/k) to negative logits and leaves the positive unchanged. Its partition estimate does not yield an unbiased finite-sample log-loss or gradient, and cannot recover excluded items. Exact gBCE is an optional alternative: -[beta*logsigmoid(s_pos)+sum(logsigmoid(-s_neg))]/(k+1), with beta=1-t+t*k/(N-1) under the paper's assumptions. History filtering changes those assumptions, so do not describe that beta as calibrated for the filtered pool without a new derivation. Match pools, k, temperature, and reductions for objective attribution.\n\nPredeclare four primary variants, validation every 10 completed epochs through the configured cap, no validation-driven early stopping, and ties resolved by earlier checkpoint followed by a fixed variant order: baseline, objective-only, residual-only, combined. Enforce the shared cumulative 43,200 GPU-second limit across all slots, training, diagnostics, debugging, and failures. Use matched cumulative time caps and log incomplete runs; 200 epochs is a cap, not a substitute for compute accounting. Run optional controls only after primary comparisons and only within remaining budget. Record category HR@10, macro HR@10, every validation query, runtime, and incumbent-versus-budget traces. The host's pinned evaluator remains authoritative.\n\nWhere the host exposes per-user validation hits, retain them and bootstrap 200 users with replacement independently within each category, using iden