Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The supplied code diagnoses item embeddings and positive-versus-negative scores 
through a SASRec-compatible interface. Model internals are not provided. 
`log2feats(sequence)` produces sequence features, and `predict_score(features, 
items)` scores candidates at each sequence position. The probe does not 
explicitly extract a final user representation; it evaluates all positions with 
nonzero positive targets.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(model, device)` stores the model/view plus `meta_data`, 
`review_data`, and `user_train`; the latter two are unused. It accesses 
`item_emb.weight`, `log2feats`, `predict_score`, and `eval()`.

The training loader supplies `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` batches of 
shape B × L. Diagnosis processes at most ten batches, switches scoring to 
evaluation mode, and disables gradients.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Sample up to 2,048 nonpadding item embeddings using 
seed 42, normalize them, and compute mean off-diagonal cosine similarity. Map 
this mean to [0,1]. Higher values indicate stronger directional alignment; 
approximately 0.5 corresponds to mean cosine zero. Lower alignment does not 
establish recommendation diversity.
- **Positive–negative separation:** Score each supplied positive and negative, 
compute their logit difference, and retain positions whose positive ID is 
nonzero. Report the mean, empirical 10th percentile, fraction below zero, and 
fraction below 0.5. Larger margins and lower failure fractions indicate better 
sampled training separation.
- **Category breakdown:** Count category occurrences separately for positive and
negative items in low-margin and wrong-rank cases, retaining the top 20 
categories per group. Counts are not normalized by category frequency. Item 
categories are unavailable in this task, so these lists remain empty when 
metadata follows the stated contract.

# Perturbation & Tests

There are no sequence perturbations, shuffling, or sensitivity tests. Random 
embedding subsampling estimates alignment; supplied negative items test pairwise
discrimination.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`, containing five
scalar metrics and a nested category breakdown. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` 
embeds both dictionaries and requests JSON with `status`, `core_findings`, 
`key_implications`, and `evidence`; it does not generate that interpretation 
itself.

Diagnosis does not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog ranking, temporal 
sensitivity, simulator traits, or recommendation diversity. Missing margin 
observations produce zeros, which can resemble healthy failure rates. Evaluation
mode is not restored afterward.

