      - Definitions: {"Movies_and_TV:embedding_collapse_score": "(mean off-diagonal cosine + 1)/2 on up to 2048 nonpadding item embeddings, isolated seed 42. Directional alignment only; 0.5 means mean cosine zero. Does not measure recommendation diversity or embedding rank.", "Movies_and_TV:pos_neg_margin_mean": "Mean positive-minus-sampled-negative logit over nonpadding pairs from at most ten loader batches and 256 sequences, further limited to reserve the frozen paired panel. In-sample, dependent on loader sampling, and scoped to the primary view rather than a four-category macro.", "Movies_and_TV:pos_neg_margin_p10": "Nearest-rank lower tenth percentile of sampled margins.", "Movies_and_TV:pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate": "Fraction of sampled margins strictly below zero.", "Movies_and_TV:pos_neg_small_margin_rate": "Fraction of sampled margins below 0.5; raw score scale affects this measurement.", "Movies_and_TV:pos_neg_margin_count": "Number of valid sampled positive-negative positions; missing estimates are null.", "Movies_and_TV:pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown": "Unsupported: item categories are unavailable. Empty category lists are not evidence of no category effects.", "Movies_and_TV:rank_change": "Perturbed target rank minus original rank; positive is worse. Diagnostic ranks use score descending, item ID ascending ties.", "Movies_and_TV:hit10_change": "Perturbed indicator(target rank <= 10) minus original indicator, within the same 100 diagnostic candidates.", "Movies_and_TV:top10_overlap": "Size of original/perturbed top-ten set intersection divided by ten.", "Movies_and_TV:feature_cosine": "Cosine between final-position features; null when either feature has zero norm.", "Movies_and_TV:aggregation": "Replicates averaged within each user, users averaged within each category, then all four required categories equally. Missing categories produce null macro entries; truncation suppresses the macro entirely.", "Movies_and_TV:ci95": "1000 paired user-bootstrap re