Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

Diagnosis accesses the item embedding table through `item_emb.weight` and 
sequence representations through `log2feats(sequence)`. Model internals are not 
supplied, so the encoder architecture and representation computation cannot be 
established. The probe uses features for every sequence position; it does not 
explicitly extract a final user representation.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(model, device)` stores the supplied model or compatibility view,
plus its `meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`. Only metadata is 
subsequently queried; reviews and stored histories are unused.

`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` invokes two probes. Training batches supply 
`(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with shape `B × L`. Sequences are 
converted to NumPy before `log2feats`; positive and negative IDs are stacked 
into `B × L × 2` candidates for `predict_score(features, items)`. Positions with
positive ID zero are excluded.

# Probes & Metrics

- **`embedding_collapse_score`:** Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding item embeddings
using seed 42, normalizes them, averages off-diagonal pairwise cosine 
similarities, and maps the mean to `[0,1]`. Higher values suggest directional 
collapse; approximately 0.5 corresponds to near-zero average cosine.
- **`pos_neg_margin_mean` / `pos_neg_margin_p10`:** Mean and lower 
tenth-percentile positive-minus-negative score across up to ten batches. Higher 
values indicate stronger separation, including difficult positions.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`:** Fraction of margins below zero; lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`:** Fraction of margins below 0.5; lower 
indicates fewer weakly separated pairs.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`:** Counts category occurrences 
separately for positive and negative items in low-margin and wrong-ranking 
cases, retaining the top 20 categories.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, input perturbation, or sensitivity tests occur. Negative 
candidates come directly from the loader. Margin evaluation disables gradients 
and sets evaluation mode without restoring the previous mode.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The returned dictionary contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. 
`diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` embeds both into instructions requesting a 
downstream JSON interpretation with status, findings, implications, and 
evidence.

These probes assess embedding geometry and sampled training-pair separation, not
validation HR@10, full-catalog ranking, or causal sequence sensitivity. Margins 
depend on score scale and negative sampling. Empty observations yield zeros that
can appear healthy. Category metadata is unavailable in this task, so category 
lists remain empty; no category information should be invented.

