Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The module accesses the trained network through `view.model`; its architecture 
is not shown. Diagnosis uses `view.item_emb.weight`, `log2feats(sequence)`, and 
`predict_score(features, items)`. History probes select `log2feats(sequence)[:, 
-1, :]` as the final sequence representation and score 100 candidates.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` consumes 
training histories and batches `(None, sequence, positive, negative)` with 
matching B × L tensors. Dataset routing requires an explicit category name or 
`diagnostic_views` mapping across the four required datasets.

Actual modules temporarily enter evaluation mode; training modes and Python, 
NumPy, and Torch RNG states are restored afterward. Frozen manifests retain 
selected users, candidates, perturbations, and seeds under 
`working/diagnostics`.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding alignment:** Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding embeddings and returns
`(mean pairwise cosine + 1)/2`. Higher values indicate stronger directional 
alignment; 0.5 means zero mean cosine. This does not establish collapse, rank, 
or recommendation diversity.
- **Positive–negative margins:** Measures positive-minus-negative logits at 
valid training positions. Reports count, mean, lower tenth percentile, 
negative-wins rate, and fraction below 0.5. Larger margins and fewer reversals 
indicate better sampled training separation; absolute thresholds depend on score
scale. This probe covers the primary view.
- **History sensitivity:** Reports target-rank change, hit@10 change, top-ten 
overlap, and final-feature cosine. Positive rank change means deterioration; 
sensitivity itself has no universally desirable direction.

# Perturbation & Tests

Up to 32 users/category contribute their final training interaction as target, 
paired with 99 unique negatives. Histories undergo oldest deletion, recent 
deletion, five random deletions, and five shuffles preserving the final item. 
Deletions compact and right-align survivors, changing positions; recent deletion
also changes the final conditioning item.

Repeated unchanged-history scoring checks determinism. User-bootstrap intervals 
summarize paired effects. Encoding is capped at 2,048 sequences with a 30-second
local time cap.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The returned object contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`: 
embedding/margin measurements, per-category and macro perturbation summaries, 
replicate records, controls, eligibility, accounting, and an unexecuted 
intervention plan. Missing category measurements yield null macro entries; 
budget truncation suppresses the macro.

Item-category breakdowns and position-preserving controls are unsupported. 
Small, in-sample panels do not establish validation HR@10, causal effects, or 
training-seed robustness. Unavailable metadata and simulator traits are not 
measured. `diagnosis_interpreter_prompt` formats these measurements and 
definitions into instructions for a separate JSON interpretation.

