{
  "description": "Strengthen the matched history-removal probe into a reproducible descriptive audit, separating compact-deletion sensitivity from positional effects and explicitly distinguishing training-example measurements from genuine auxiliary generalization experiments.",
  "motivation": "Current probes measure embedding geometry and sampled training discrimination without testing history dependence. Controlled perturbations can reveal reliance on particular events, but neither sensitivity nor qualitative feedback establishes useful preference modeling. The revised proposal preserves the inexpensive early-stage audit while removing unsupported holdout and predictive-validity claims.",
  "implementation_notes": "Preserve DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Access the trained network through view.model and retain compatibility scoring hooks, existing geometry probes, and sampled-margin probes. Restore every module's prior training flag with try/finally. Use only public histories, timestamps, titles, and descriptions; do not read unavailable reviews, ratings, categories, prices, stores, or simulator traits. Treat functional fit as supported/contradicted/unknown with explicit text evidence; do not convert unobserved prerequisites into incompatibility or uncertain recommendations into dislikes. For the inexpensive audit, reserve the final training event as an inference target while explicitly labeling it previously observed during model fitting. Freeze its preceding history after truncation to the model context, before interventions; never refill deleted positions from older history. Require at least three retained events so the terminal occurrence, latest nonterminal treatment occurrence, and a distinct nonterminal control occurrence exist. Delete occurrence indices rather than all instances of an item. Sample controls uniformly with replacement across draws from indices excluding both the terminal and treatment occurrences; retain and report the index draws, repetition, item-frequency distributions, eligible counts, and short-history exclusions. Repeat five controls per user using independent deterministic RNG streams derived from seed 42 and stable dataset/user identifiers. Match deletion count and original history length within users; repetition/frequency matching is an optional separately labeled analysis that must report eligibility losses and residual imbalance. Compact deletion rebuilds left-padded inputs and shifts surviving earlier events; this remains a confound. The stronger position-preserving intervention must preserve surviving absolute positions, block the removed occurrence as a key/value in every attention layer, keep the terminal query, and pass mask checks. A zero item embedding alone is insufficient because positional signals can survive. If the architecture cannot support this intervention through a verified adapter, return null with the reason rather than approximate it with padding. Neither intervention has a predetermined desirable sensitivity direction. For each user, sample 99 unique auxiliary negatives from the dataset's item universe, excluding all items in that user's prescribed training history; use the same candidates and tie rule for every treatment. Mark users ineligible when fewer than 99 eligible negatives exist. Report target-rank changes, HR@10 changes, candidate-set top-10 overlap, and recent-minus-mean-control differences with explicit signs and definitions. Treat unavailable values as null, never healthy zeros. Bound the audit to a deterministic maximum of 200 eligible training users per category, sampling uniformly without replacement from users sorted by stable ID; preserve all four dataset routes. Aggregate user outcomes within categories before equally averaging categories, and return null for the four-category macro if any category is unavailable. Bootstrap paired user vectors within categories using 1,000 draws and seed 42; calculate percentile intervals for the category and equally weighted macro differences. These intervals exclude training-seed variation, diagnostic-user sampling uncertainty beyond the empirical bootstrap, and adaptive selection bias. For genuinely held-out auxiliary targets, predeclare suffix sizes or a timestamp cutoff before fitting separate diagnostic models from fresh initialization; exclude suffixes from input sequences, positive targets, and interaction-derived statistics. Declare the auxiliary item universe and negative-sampling distribution explicitly; a globally future claim requires all training interactions and derived statistics to precede the common cutoff, with training-vocabulary eligibility reported. Do not fine-tune a contaminated checkpoint and call it target exclusion. Auxiliary splits are derived exclusively from prescribed training data and do not alter official splits. Predictive-validity experiments are optional later work: predefine probes and a gain-prediction rule on development variants, freeze the rule, and evaluate previously unseen architecture/loss/sampler families against measured pinned validation HR@10 changes. Compare incremental prediction against popularity, last-item, recency-weighted pairwise scores, and rank-based margins; report Spearman correlation, gain-sign accuracy with zero-gain handling, and uncertainty. These are proposed experiments, not established effects. Predeclare a bounded trial count, record every trial and GPU cost within the shared 43,200 GPU-second budget, and acknowledge adaptive validation overfitting. Keep DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, all four categories, the environment's SASREC_EPOCHS=200 default, and the host evaluator unchanged. Write artifacts beneath the trial directory. Full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for the twenty real training users remain separate diagnostics. The selected audit changes no production inference architecture; any later pairwise residual or architecture change must also update the predictor writer and working/predict.py.",
  "pseudocode": "save every module's training flag\ntry:\n  set view.model to evaluation mode\n  under no_grad:\n    for each of the four routed datasets:\n      deterministically select at most 200 eligible training users\n      for each user:\n        target = final prescribed-training occurrence\n        window = truncate preceding occurrences BEFORE perturbation\n        require len(window) >= 3\n        terminal_index = len(window) - 1\n        treatment_index = len(window) - 2\n        control_pool = indices excluding terminal_index and treatment_index\n        sample five control indices with replacement using stable seeded RNG\n        candidates = target + 99 fixed unique auxiliary negatives\n        score unmodified window\n        for treatment_index and each sampled control index:\n          compact = delete that occurrence and rebuild left-padded window\n          score compact using the same candidates\n          if verified architecture-aware position-preserving masking exists:\n            retain surviving absolute position IDs\n            block removed occurrence as a key/value at every layer\n            score masked window at the unchanged terminal occurrence\n          else:\n            record position-preserving result as null with reason\n        record ranks, HR@10 indicators, top-10 overlaps, and paired effects\n        record repetition, item frequencies, removed indices, and zero overlap\n      aggregate paired user vectors and eligibility counts within category\n    average the four category means only when all are available\n    bootstrap paired users within categories for 1,000 seed-42 replicates\nfinally:\n  restore every module's saved training flag\nreturn {metrics, metric_definitions}\n\ninterpreter prompt:\n  embed measured values, definitions, counts, missingness, and controls\n  label previously trained targets as descriptive training examples\n  explain positional confounding and candidate dependence\n  prohibit causal preference claims and unsupported gain predictions\n\noptional later auxiliary experiment:\n  predeclare training-only chronological suffixes/cutoff\n  fit separate diagnostic models from fresh initialization on allowed prefixes\n  exclude reserved suffixes from supervision and interaction statistics\n  evaluate only targets absent from fitting\n  freeze gain-prediction rules before testing unseen variant families",
