{
  "description": "A position-controlled recency audit prospectively tests whether baseline recent-versus-older history sensitivity predicts gains from a fixed later-target-weighted SASRec objective. Evaluate a frozen diagnostic deployment rule against always-baseline and always-variant policies across all four categories.",
  "motivation": "The existing deletion probes mix content changes with position and final-item changes. More fundamentally, later-target loss weighting changes which prefix–target examples receive emphasis, rather than directly increasing reliance on recent conditioning items. Retaining this inexpensive intervention is appropriate at 10% progress only with a narrow predictive hypothesis and explicit separation from causal claims about recency.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Return metrics and metric_definitions including eligibility, matching quality, replicate variability, uncertainty, controls, and limitations. Access the trained module through view.model and preserve compatible embedding, feature, and scoring hooks. Preserve each module's training flag and Python, NumPy, CPU Torch, and CUDA RNG states; use local diagnostic generators and no_grad.\n\nBefore examining variant outcomes, freeze an executable manifest. Previously inspected results remain retrospective evidence. Use preprocessing seed 0 and training seed 42. Select up to 32 eligible training users per category by a local seed-0 permutation of sorted user IDs. Hold out each user's final training item only for diagnostic scoring, removing it from the conditioning prefix without changing training splits. This target was fitted during SASRec training and must be labeled accordingly. Require a prefix of at least five items, right-aligned within the model's maximum length. Keep its final conditioning item unchanged. Define the recent editable position as the penultimate occupied position and the older editable position as the earliest occupied position. Record their distances from the end and report length strata; this design does not independently identify absolute-position effects.\n\nUse one target and 99 unique negatives per user, drawn from category-local item IDs excluding padding and all that user's training interactions. Freeze candidates across paired edits. Where fewer than 99 eligible negatives exist, mark the user ineligible. These are training diagnostic candidate sets, separate from the host's validation sets. For each editable position, exclude the original item and target from replacement eligibility. Match whether the replacement already appears elsewhere in the prefix. Among eligible items, minimize squared differences in standardized log1p training frequency and baseline embedding norm; standardize over nonpadding category items, clamping standard deviations below 1e-8. Sample five distinct replacements uniformly from the 50 closest eligible items, or all eligible items when fewer exist. Record shortages, distances, and duplicate-count changes; matching repetition presence does not preserve exact multiplicity. Freeze baseline norms and replacements for any later model comparisons. Frequency/norm matching is a proposed partial control, not an established guarantee of realistic transitions. Preserve sequence shape, occupied positions, padding, candidate identities, and any timestamp slots. Add repeated unchanged scoring and a swap of the recent and older positions, preserving the item multiset and final item. Explicitly distinguish identity replacement from position swapping.\n\nRank targets with deterministic item-ID tie breaking. Define each replacement effect as (edited target rank minus unchanged target rank)/99. Average draws within user, then users within category. Let D_c equal mean recent effect minus mean older effect. The frozen prediction is that larger D_c corresponds to larger category HR@10 gain. The fixed policy chooses the variant when D_c > 0 and baseline otherwise; ties select baseline. This sign and threshold are proposed design choices, not empirically validated values. If any category lacks an eligible diagnostic panel, declare the four-category policy analysis unavailable rather than inventing a diagnostic value.\n\nFor valid training positions, use w_ut = exp[-lambda(T_u-t)], lambda = log(2)/10, where T_u is the last valid target position in that sampled sequence. Compute loss as sum(m*w*(positive BCE + negative BCE))/sum(m*w). Use the same reduction with w=1 for the control, and establish that it reproduces the starting objective's scaling before comparison. The ten-position half-life is fixed before outcomes; it is not a tuned optimum. Keep sampler, optimizer, architecture, and training schedule identical. Later targets often have longer prefixes, so a benefit cannot be attributed solely to recency. Honor the SASREC_EPOCHS environment value, normally 200. Use the existing checkpoint convention identically without adding extra validation-driven tuning.\n\nTrain both models for all four categories on a single GPU. Account for all eight category fits, diagnostics, debugging, and failed runs within 43,200 GPU-seconds. Reuse a baseline only when its code, seed, schedule, and artifacts match exactly; classify already inspected evidence transparently. Maintain a shared budget ledger and stop before exceeding it; report an incomplete experiment if the full matrix cannot fit. Concurrency must not silently exceed the method-wide budget.\n\nObtain unchanged host validation outcomes. If paired per-user hit indicators are exposed by the host, compute variant-minus-baseline hit differences, category means, equally weighted macro gain, and both discordant counts. Use 10,000 seed-0 paired user-bootstrap resamples separately within each category, with percentile 95% intervals. These condition on trained models and fixed candidates; they exclude seed variation and adaptive-selection correction. If only aggregate HR@10 is exposed, report aggregate comparisons and mark paired intervals and discordant counts unavailable; never modify the evaluator or reconstruct hidden labels.\n\nReport the fixed policy, always-baseline, and always-variant macro values. Prespecify Spearman association between D_c and category gains using average ranks for ties; constant inputs make association undefined. Enumerate all 24 permutations of category diagnostic assignments and recompute both association and policy improvement over always-baseline. Report exact fractions of permutations at least as large as observed, including the observed assignment. Treat them as exploratory correspondence checks: exchangeability across heterogeneous categories is questionable, minimum attainable one-sided probability is 1/24, and users are not independent category-level observations. One variant cannot establish optimal intervention selection or general diagnostic usefulness.\n\nKeep DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], all four dataset routes, and all artifacts under the trial directory. Keep the predictor writer synchronized; this loss-only variant uses the unchanged inference architecture. Produce full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for five real training users per category as required, without interpreting these as catalog accuracy measurements. Use only histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps. Ratings, reviews, item categories, prices, stores, simulator traits, compatibility, and replacement intent are unavailable unless supported by permitted evidence. The pinned macro validation HR@10 remains the selection objective. Additional validation perturbation studies or candidate-seed audits are outside this narrow experiment unless explicitly supported and budgeted; hidden test files remain untouched.",
  "pseudocode": "freeze design before variant outcomes:\n    seeds = {preprocessing: 0, training: 42, diagnostics: 0, bootstrap: 0}\n    lambda = log(2)/10; threshold = 0; replacement_replicates = 5\n    freeze eligible users, diagnostic candidates, matching rule, controls, analysis\n\nfit or verify exact baseline for every required category\nsave module modes and RNG states\ntry:\n    set baseline view.model to eval\n    under no_grad:\n        for category in required_categories:\n            build frozen fitted-target diagnostic panel\n            for user in panel:\n                score unchanged prefix twice\n                replace penultimate and earliest occupied items separately\n                preserve final item, occupied positions, candidates, and padding\n                score five frozen matched replacements per edit\n                score recent/older position swap\n                record rank effects, overlap, feature cosine, and matching residuals\n            D[category] = mean_user(recent_rank_effect - older_rank_effect)\nfinally:\n    restore module modes and RNG states\nreturn {metrics, metric_definitions}\n\nfreeze D and diagnostic deployment choices before observing variant results\nfor category in required_categories:\n    train variant with otherwise identical configuration and seed 42:\n        valid = positive != 0\n        T = final valid target position per sequence\n        w = exp(-lambda * (T - position)) on valid positions\n        loss = sum(valid*w*(positive_BCE + negative_BCE)) / sum(valid*w)\n    obtain pinned host validation outcomes\n\nreport category and equal-category macro HR@10 gains\nreport policy(D > 0), always-baseline, and always-variant values\nif paired user hits are available:\n    report discordant counts and stratified paired bootstrap intervals\nif all four diagnostic values and gains are available:\n    compute prespecified Spearman association\n    enumerate all 24 diagnostic-to-category assignments\n    report exploratory association and policy correspondence checks\nlog all outcomes, missingness, validation queries, and budget consumption\n\ndef diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis):\n    format measured metrics, definitions, controls, eligibility, and limitations\n    distinguish fitted-target sensitivity from validation improvement\n    explain that later-target weighting does not directly impose conditioning recency\n    request testable interpretations without inferring unobserved preferences\n    return prompt",
