Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

Only diagnosis code is supplied; model internals cannot be verified. The adapter
exposes the trained module as `view.model`, item embeddings through 
`view.item_emb`, sequence features through `log2feats(sequence)`, and candidate 
logits through `predict_score(features, items)`. Paired probes use 
`log2feats(sequence)[:, -1, :]` as the final user representation after 
zero-left-padding the history.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` accesses public training histories and explicit 
dataset routes for the four required categories. The loader supplies matching B 
× L sequence, positive-item, and negative-item tensors. `run_full_diagnosis` 
temporarily switches actual modules to evaluation mode and restores module modes
and global RNG states afterward. Scoring probes disable gradients.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding alignment:** Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding embeddings and 
computes `(mean pairwise cosine + 1)/2`. Values near 1 indicate strong 
directional alignment; 0.5 means zero average cosine. This does not establish 
representation rank or recommendation diversity.
- **Positive–negative margins:** Scores sampled training pairs at valid 
positions. Reports count, mean, lower tenth percentile, fraction below zero, and
fraction below 0.5. Larger positive margins and fewer inversions indicate better
sampled-pair separation; raw score scale affects interpretation.
- **History sensitivity:** Measures target rank change, hit@10 change, top-ten 
overlap, and final-feature cosine. Positive rank change means worse ranking; 
negative hit change means lost hits. Sensitivity itself is neither inherently 
good nor bad.

# Perturbation & Tests

A saved deterministic manifest selects up to 32 users/category, each with a 
final training interaction as target and 99 unique negatives. Tests delete 
oldest or recent items, randomly delete items across five replicates, or shuffle
earlier items while preserving the last item across five replicates. Deletions 
compact histories and alter positions. Repeated unchanged-history scoring checks
determinism. Position-preserving controls are unsupported.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The result contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. Metrics include 
embedding/margin summaries, nested `history_perturbations`, an unexecuted 
`intervention_experiment` plan, and diagnostic accounting. Perturbations retain 
user records, controls, coverage, per-category summaries, and four-category 
macro estimates with 1,000 user-bootstrap intervals.

The 2,048-sequence/30-second caps can truncate coverage and suppress macro 
results. Margins concern the primary view only. Targets are in-sample; intervals
exclude training-seed variability and adaptive-selection bias. Item-category 
breakdowns are unavailable. No held-out performance, simulator traits, causal 
benefit, or intervention improvement is established.

